    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d905">

                <pb facs="1034" n="922" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg922"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.6363/202a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-07-17T16:00:00-04:00">July 17, 1935—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>110. Your 151, July 16, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="18" xml:id="d905-f1"/> last paragraph,
                    and Department’s 109, July 16, 8 p.m.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d905-f2"/> As
                    Standard-Vacuum has indicated to Department continued concern with regard to
                    carrying out by Japanese authorities of assurances given orally in reference to
                    petroleum regulation in Japan, Department suggests that in your discretion you
                    mention this subject in the course of your final talk with the Foreign
                    Minister.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
